# Normalise to LF in the repository. The daily refresh Action runs on Ubuntu and the
# development checkout is Windows; without this, every scheduled data commit would show
# as a whole-file rewrite.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shims must keep CRLF or cmd.exe can mis-parse them.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Emitted data is machine-written, single-line JSON. Never merge it by hand -- rebuild.
#
# `merge=ours` was NOT doing that. `ours` is not a built-in merge driver and no `merge.ours.*`
# driver is configured here, so git silently fell back to the ordinary text three-way driver and
# wrote `<<<<<<< HEAD` conflict markers INTO snapshot.json. `-diff` then hid them, because
# `git diff` prints only "Binary files differ" for these paths -- so a human resolving the merge
# would see nothing wrong and commit a payload with conflict markers in it.
#
# `-merge` is the real thing: git refuses to auto-merge, flags the conflict and leaves our
# version in the worktree. The instruction above is now enforced rather than asserted.
data/processed/** -diff -merge linguist-generated
web/public/data/** -diff -merge linguist-generated
